# Evidence reading quality

When the assigned question or the reading priorities ask how something is produced, derived or decided, read the complete passage that defines it and follow the chain from its origin to its result within the materials granted to this stage. Record that chain in the Note step by step, and check every named element against the lines you cite. Record what the Source actually states or does; a name, label, heading, comment or summary is a lead to verify, not evidence of what happens. In code, this means reading the complete relevant functions and following their inputs, assignments, called modules and configuration. For each conclusion about a value's origin, write its assignment chain from the original input and check the named operands against the cited lines. Preserve the actual input representation, length source and tensor layout; do not substitute what the algorithm's name or a comment suggests.

Distinguish what is in effect from what is only available: a default, an example and the option actually selected are different facts, and the Note says which of them it reports. When the Source does not show which one applies, describe the alternatives conditionally. A surface match, such as the same name, size or wording, does not establish that two things correspond. Separate what the Source establishes from what you assume. In code, this means including the implementation branches enabled by the selected configuration, and distinguishing constructor defaults, example configurations and the configuration actually selected by the caller. Separate equal tensor lengths from semantic alignment, and distinguish code-derived shapes from assumptions. An omitted Note or excerpt does not establish that the available Source lacks the detail.

Keep conclusions tied to the Source and version actually read. When combining materials within this stage's scope, identify their distinct origins and verify the connection between them before transferring a fact from one to another; one matching part does not establish that the wholes agree. In code, one matching function or file does not establish that their callers and configuration agree, so verify the relevant call chain. Preserve meaningful disagreements rather than silently merging them.

When compressing a Note, retain the chains, branch conditions, selections and qualifications needed for the requested detail. Concision must not remove evidence needed to reconstruct a conclusion. Stay within the stage's assigned Source scope; a limitation of these materials is not a judgment about other Sources or global coverage.
